What was modified
-----------------

Only files served to the browser (web-apps, two constants and nothing else
in sdkjs). The server, converter and binaries are unchanged. Each changed
file carries a "Modified by Drylab" line stating the change and its date.
The scripts below run in the Dockerfile; each fails the build if its anchor
is not found exactly once.

1. Added web-apps/apps/common/main/resources/drylab/drylab.css (source:
   drylab-theme/drylab.css): a light theme for the "White" interface
   theme (flat header and tabs, one-row toolbar, soft canvas, smaller and
   muted but always visible ONLYOFFICE logo, Sheets/Slides-style grid,
   formula bar, sheet tabs and speaker notes, Drylab green accent). It also
   adds a line to ONLYOFFICE's About panel stating that this is a modified
   version, by whom, that it is based on ONLYOFFICE Docs by Ascensio System
   SIA, the licence and where this source is.

2. web-apps/apps/{documenteditor,spreadsheeteditor,presentationeditor}/
   main/index.html: one <link> to drylab.css (scripts/patch-index.sh).

3. sdkjs/cell/sdk-all.js: two colour constants, the cell grid lines
   (rgb 202,202,202 -> 226,227,227) and the selection outline
   (rgb 72,121,92 -> 0,157,81) (scripts/patch-js.sh).

4. web-apps/apps/spreadsheeteditor/main/app/controller/Main.js: one event
   listener, so the public API call docEditor.blurFocus() also closes the
   cell editor the way clicking another cell does; a cell still being typed
   in is kept when the integrator saves (scripts/patch-js.sh).

5. web-apps/apps/{documenteditor,spreadsheeteditor,presentationeditor}/
   main/app/template/LeftMenu.template and .../main/app/view/LeftMenu.js:
   one "About" button at the bottom of the left strip. Its click calls the
   public Gateway's internalMessage('drylab:about'), which asks the
   integrator page to show its About dialog; it sends no document data
   (scripts/patch-about.sh).

6. The precompressed (.gz) copies of the touched files are regenerated so
   the server never serves a stale stock copy.

7. Hidden by drylab.css (no Community configuration key exists for them):
   the Collaboration tab, the users counter, the Editing/Viewing switch, the
   header close button, the header avatar, search and Share, and
   ONLYOFFICE's own About entry in the left strip (its place is taken by the
   button in 5).

Where the legal notices are shown
---------------------------------

In every editor (document, spreadsheet, presentation) there is an
"About" (i) button at the bottom of its left strip. It opens the integrating
application's About dialog, which identifies ONLYOFFICE Docs by Ascensio
System SIA as the original software, states that this is a modified
version, and gives access to the licence and to this source. The
ONLYOFFICE logo stays visible in the menu row, and ONLYOFFICE's About panel
itself is not removed from the program.

Nothing else was changed. ONLYOFFICE's copyright notices, licence notices,
source file headers and logo are kept.

